;
; DEED clause profile: the edict form of a contractile-deed, v1.0.0 (DRAFT)
; Prose and rationale: docs/estate-reconciliation/A7-contractiles-descriptiles-anchor.adoc
; sections 8.1 (the edict), 8.4 (strictness and "!"), 8.5 (the Bust use
; envelope); rulings W2, W7, W10, J5, J13, J17, J20. M3 module order: section 11.
;
; A CLAUSE PROFILE, not a new grammar. Every rule below is also a `clause` of
; deed.abnf v1.5.0 (the bang included), so an edict file still passes
; deed_lint unchanged. Rules it borrows: string, value, field, token-sep and
; bang are deed.abnf's; str-list is common.abnf's; verb-name is
; contractiles.abnf's. Requires RFC 7405 (%s"..." case-sensitive literals).
;
; Where it applies: a <Verb>file.deed (head contractile-deed, J14), at the top
; level of the form. SEMANTIC (validator-enforced, deed_lint.js --edict):
;   * the form carries :schema-version, :canonical-name (a string), :of-chora
;     (the repo's version 8 chora id, #uuid or #u8, J20, J28) and :verb (a
;     verb-name), each exactly once, and no :beholding-chora (J20);
;   * :verb agrees with the file name (Intentfile.deed is intend, Mustfile.deed
;     is must, and so on; A7 8.1);
;   * every other top-level member is an edict-rule, or, in a Bustfile only,
;     at most one bust-envelope (8.5).

edict-rule      = "(" %s"rule" 1*(token-sep edict-member) [token-sep] ")"
                ; SEMANTIC: :id, :text, (applies-when …) and (requires …)
                ; each exactly once. The :id is unique in the file, is an A5
                ; name segment (1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "." / "_" / "-")), and
                ; "contractile/<verb>/<id>" is at most 200 characters (A5 3.1,
                ; J13). :text is not empty.
edict-member    = id-member / text-member / applies-when / requires
id-member       = %s":id" token-sep string [token-sep bang]
                ; "!" marks a blocking rule (J17, 8.4). SEMANTIC: refused in
                ; an Intentfile, which keeps room to explore (8.4); implied,
                ; and so optional, in a Mustfile.
text-member     = %s":text" token-sep string

applies-when    = "(" %s"applies-when" token-sep selector [token-sep] ")"
                ; What a rule applies to, tested against the chora (A1
                ; identity; A2 profile and capabilities) and, where a rule
                ; needs it, context such as a path or a deployment (8.1).
selector        = always-selector / field-selector
always-selector = "(" %s"always" [token-sep] ")"
field-selector  = "(" selector-head 1*(token-sep field) [token-sep] ")"
                ; Every field must hold (a conjunction). SEMANTIC: no field
                ; repeats, and no field carries a bang.
selector-head   = %s"identity" / %s"profile" / %s"capabilities" / %s"context"
                ; There is no clade selector: a placement is an identity
                ; fact, but no edict hangs off the clade (W10, 8.1).

requires        = "(" %s"requires" token-sep requirement [token-sep] ")"
requirement     = "(" verb-name 1*(token-sep requirement-member) [token-sep] ")"
                ; SEMANTIC: the head is the deed's :verb; :witness appears
                ; exactly once and equals the rule's own :id (J5: a fact names
                ; the edict it witnesses); exactly one of :value, :at-least
                ; and :at-most appears.
requirement-member = ( %s":witness" token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":value" token-sep value )
                   / ( %s":at-least" token-sep value )
                   / ( %s":at-most" token-sep value )

bust-envelope   = "(" %s"envelope" 1*(token-sep envelope-member) [token-sep] ")"
                ; What the repo is fit for and not fit for; Bust severity is
                ; scored inside it (8.5). SEMANTIC: Bustfile.deed only, at
                ; most once, each member at most once.
envelope-member = ( %s":for" token-sep str-list )
                / ( %s":not-for" token-sep str-list )
                / ( %s":tolerance" token-sep string )
